[compat-oai] maxOutputTokens is ignored (not mapped to max_tokens)

The @genkit-ai/compat-oai plugin (OpenAI Compatible) ignores the maxOutputTokens configuration field. It correctly destructures it from the Genkit configuration but fails to map it to the max_tokens field in the OpenAI request body. As a result, requests are often capped at the model's or provider's default limit (e.g., 2048 tokens), even when a higher limit is requested.

Location: The issue occurs in the toOpenAIRequestBody function in js/plugins/compat-oai/src/model.ts.

Analysis: In the compiled code (
node_modules/@genkit-ai/compat-oai/lib/model.js
):
```
const {
  temperature,
  maxOutputTokens,  // <--- 1. Destructured here
  // ...
  ...restOfConfig   // <--- 2. It's excluded from restOfConfig
} = request.config ?? {};

let body = {
  // ...
  temperature,
  // <--- BUG: max_tokens is missing here!
};

if (requestBuilder) {
  requestBuilder(request, body);
} else {
  // 3. Since it was destructured, it's NOT in restOfConfig either
  body = { ...body, ...restOfConfig }; 
}
```

Steps to Reproduce:

Use the openAICompatible plugin with any OpenAI-compatible provider (e.g., Fireworks AI).
Invoke a model with maxOutputTokens set to a high value (e.g., 32768).
Observe that the response is truncated at the provider's default limit (e.g., 2048 tokens).
Expected Behavior: maxOutputTokens should be mapped to max_tokens in the OpenAI request body.

Environment:

Genkit version: 1.28.0
@genkit-ai/compat-oai version: 1.28.0

