@ai-sdk/anthropic: reasoning on adaptive-thinking models returns thinking blocks with no text

`ai@7.0.37`, `@ai-sdk/anthropic@4.0.20`

On models that use adaptive thinking (Sonnet 5, Opus 4.6+), setting the provider-agnostic `reasoning` option produces thinking blocks whose text is empty. `resolveAnthropicReasoningConfig` returns `{ thinking: { type: 'adaptive' }, effort }` and never sets `thinking.display`, so Anthropic's default of `"omitted"` applies — the model thinks, the tokens are billed, and the text is stripped. The provider's own schema documents `"summarized"` as "Required to see reasoning output".

```ts
const result = streamText({
  model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-5'),
  reasoning: 'high',
  prompt: '<something that needs real deliberation>',
});
// reasoning-delta chunks: 0
// add providerOptions: { anthropic: { thinking: { type: 'adaptive', display: 'summarized' } } }
// reasoning-delta chunks: 58, with text
```

Same code on `claude-sonnet-4-5` (non-adaptive, legacy budget path) streams reasoning normally, so this only affects the newer models.

The OpenAI provider handles the equivalent case: when `reasoning` is set it defaults `reasoningSummary` to `"detailed"`. Anthropic's mapping doing the same for `display` would make the generic option behave consistently across providers. Failing that, a warning would help — today it's a 200 with a signed but empty thinking block and nothing pointing at the missing flag.

[Epic 10] Story 10.5: Cross-Reference System

As a player, when two journal entries relate (Material X found on Planet Y, Language fragment Z heard in Region W), the journal surfaces that connection, so that knowledge compounds across domains.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Journal entries can have typed relationships to other entries (e.g., "found on", "combined with", "derived from", "similar to")
- [ ] Cross-references are created automatically when observations establish connections (e.g., recording a material observation on a planet links material → planet)
- [ ] Cross-references are visible in the journal detail panel as navigable links
- [ ] Player can follow a cross-reference link to jump to the related entry
- [ ] Cross-references are bidirectional — if Material X links to Planet Y, Planet Y links back to Material X
- [ ] Relationship types include at minimum: FoundOn, CombinedWith, DerivedFrom, SimilarTo, ObservedAt
- [ ] Cross-references accumulate — the same relationship strengthens with repeated evidence (confidence on edges)
- [ ] The associative web view (future — data model only in this story) can traverse cross-references via bounded BFS
- [ ] Cross-references are serializable for save/load
- [ ] No cross-reference is created without an observation event — the system never infers connections the player hasn't made

## Technical Design

### KnowledgeGraph Integration

The data-architecture decision specifies a `KnowledgeGraph` resource backed by `petgraph::Graph`. This story implements that decision for journal cross-references:

```rust
