System prompt: collapse to a single assembler and a single declared placement

## Summary

The complete system prompt is assembled twice — once in the agent layer and once again in the provider layer — and the two copies are concatenated into a single system message. Every request therefore carries two copies of the preamble, Core Mandates, global `LLXPRT.md`, project `.llxprt/LLXPRT.md`, and the core memory block. The two copies are generated at different times, so they can also disagree about which model is running.

This affects the `openai`, `openai-responses`/`codex`, `anthropic`, and `gemini` paths — all four use the same merge.

## Evidence

From a real captured request dump (`~/Library/Caches/llxprt-code/dumps/20260731-192636-openai-2t7ju3-request.json`), a single `system` message of **59,457 characters**. Structure by line number:

    line   1: You are LLxprt Code running on darwin with zai-org/GLM-5.2 via openai.
    line  19: # Core Mandates
    line 148: --- Core System Memory from: ~/Library/Preferences/llxprt-code/.LLXPRT_SYSTEM ---
    line 156: --- Context from: ../../Library/Preferences/llxprt-code/LLXPRT.md ---
    line 201: --- Context from: .llxprt/LLXPRT.md ---
    line 213: This is LLxprt Code. We are setting up the context for our chat.
    line 424: --- Context from: .llxprt/LLXPRT.md ---            <-- 2nd copy
    line 436: You are LLxprt Code running on darwin with gpt-5.5 via openai.   <-- 2nd preamble, DIFFERENT MODEL
    line 454: # Core Mandates                                     <-- 2nd copy
    line 583: --- Context from: ../../Library/Preferences/llxprt-code/.LLXPRT_SYSTEM ---
    line 591: --- Context from: ../../Library/Preferences/llxprt-code/LLXPRT.md ---   <-- 2nd copy

Marker counts in the same message:

    "You are LLxprt Code running on"      2
    "Context from: .llxprt/LLXPRT.md"     4   (2 open + 2 close)
    "LLxprt Code Added Memories"         12

The layout is `[core prompt A] + [environment context] + [core prompt B]`.

Note lines 1 and 436: **the two copies name different models** (`zai-org/GLM-5.2` and `gpt-5.5`). One copy is stale. The model is being told it is a different model than the one serving the request.

A second, independent dump (`20260731-192359-openai-vtcg72-request.json`) shows the identical structure at the identical line offsets, so this is systematic, not a one-off.

## Root cause

**Assembly 1 — agent layer.** `buildSystemInstruction` (`packages/agents/src/core/ChatSessionFactory.ts:113-154`) builds a complete system prompt and prepends the environment context:

    let systemInstruction = await getCoreSystemPromptAsync({
      userMemory, coreMemory, mcpInstructions, model,
      tools: enabledToolNames, includeSubagentDelegation, interactionMode,
    });

    const envContextText = envParts.map(...).join('\n');
    if (envContextText) {
      systemInstruction = envContextText + '\n\n' + systemInstruction;
    }

That result is stored on the session (`ChatSessionFactory.ts:407`, `chatSession.ts:546`) and reaches providers as `options.systemInstruction`.

**Assembly 2 — provider layer.** `packages/providers/src/openai/OpenAIRequestPreparation.ts:125-141` builds a *second* complete core prompt and concatenates:

    const corePrompt = await getCoreSystemPromptAsync({
      userMemory, mcpInstructions, model, tools: toolNamesArg,
      includeSubagentDelegation, interactionMode: ...,
    });
    // Issue #2410: Merge the caller-supplied system instruction (e.g. a
    // subagent persona/task prompt) with the core system prompt so the
    // instruction reaches the Chat Completions API as the system message.
    return mergeSystemInstruction(corePrompt, options.systemInstruction);

`mergeSystemInstruction` (`packages/providers/src/utils/systemInstructionMerge.ts:15-30`) is plain concatenation with no dedup:

    return `${coreText}\n\n${instructionText}`;

The comment reveals the intended contract: `options.systemInstruction` was expected to be a **caller-supplied persona or task prompt** (the subagent case from #2410). For the main a

